---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Ecommerce & Integration Solutions for Promotional Products Suppliers | Swishtag";
const description = "Shopify and integration solutions for promotional products suppliers that need cleaner product data and order connectivity.";
const canonical = "https://cms.swishtag.com/industries/promotional-products-suppliers/";
const robots = "index,follow";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} robots={robots}>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/generic-page.css" />
  <main><section class="gp-hero"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-kicker">For suppliers</div><h1>Make your product data easier for commerce teams to use.</h1><p>Supplier ecommerce projects work best when product information, order handoffs and downstream workflows are designed as one system instead of separate exports and manual steps.</p><div class="gp-actions"><a class="gp-btn primary" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a><a class="gp-btn secondary" href="/solutions/">Explore solutions</a></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-section-head"><h2>Integrate the stable process first.</h2><p>Automating a messy data model just moves the mess faster. Start with the fields, ownership and order states that are actually dependable.</p></div><div class="gp-grid"><article aria-label="Open Commerce-ready product data" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/book-demo/?industry=supplier" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>PRODUCT DATA</small><h3>Commerce-ready product data</h3><p>Structure the data needed by storefronts without making teams rebuild the same information repeatedly.</p><a href="/book-demo/?industry=supplier">Discuss product data →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Cleaner order handoff" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/book-demo/?industry=supplier" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>ORDER FLOW</small><h3>Cleaner order handoff</h3><p>Connect the order path where automation creates a reliable reduction in repeated administration.</p><a href="/book-demo/?industry=supplier">Map order flow →</a></article><article aria-label="Open Focused storefronts" class="gp-card st-clickable-card" data-card-href="/solutions/" role="link" tabindex="0"><small>SHOPIFY</small><h3>Focused storefronts</h3><p>Use Shopify for direct, dealer or program experiences when it fits the commercial model.</p><a href="/solutions/">Explore solutions →</a></article></div></div></section><section class="gp-section alt"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-split"><div><h2>What this page will cover</h2></div><div class="gp-list"><div>Identify the product data downstream buyers need.</div><div>Define where pricing and availability rules should live.</div><div>Map order acknowledgements and status changes.</div><div>Add integration only after the data contract is clear.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="gp-section"><div class="gp-wrap"><div class="gp-cta"><div><h2>Have a workflow that does not fit off-the-shelf software?</h2><p>Show us the current process. We can help identify the simplest Shopify, integration, or automation approach before you commit to a larger build.</p></div><a class="gp-btn" href="/book-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a></div><p class="gp-note">This page is connected and launch-ready. Detailed sales copy, proof, screenshots and SEO depth can be expanded in the next content pass.</p></div></section></main>
</BaseLayout>
